# lesson1 – BankAccount and Object Properties in C#

This project demonstrates encapsulation and property usage in C# through a simple `BankAccount` class.

## Concepts Covered

- Auto-properties (`OwnerName`)
- Read-only properties (`Balance`)
- Backing fields (`_balance`)
- Input validation in methods (`Deposit`, `Withdraw`, `TransferTo`)
- Constructor-based initialization
- Object-to-object interaction via public API

## Code Overview

```csharp
var alice = new BankAccount("Alice", 1000m);
var bob = new BankAccount("Bob", 500m);

alice.TransferTo(bob, 200m);

Console.WriteLine(alice.Balance); // 800
Console.WriteLine(bob.Balance);   // 700